From: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(autoware_system_monitor): build with Boost 1.87 and later

Boost 1.88 made Boost.Process v2 the default: boost/process.hpp now
declares the v2 API, and v1 lives in boost/process/v1.hpp. Code written
against v1 stops compiling ("pipe is not a member of bp").

When the v1 headers exist (Boost 1.86 and later), set
BOOST_PROCESS_VERSION=1, which makes v1 the inline namespace again so
boost::process:: names keep resolving to the v1 API, and include
boost/process/v1.hpp. Boost 1.88 has the v1 headers but not v1.hpp, so
there the headers v1.hpp would include are listed one by one. Older
Boost (Ubuntu 24.04 has 1.83) takes the #else branch and is unchanged.

The selection lives in one new header, system_monitor/boost_process.hpp,
included by every file that used boost/process.hpp.

Boost 1.87 also removed the io_service alias of io_context (an alias since
Boost 1.66) and io_context::run(error_code &). run() reports the same
errors by throwing boost::system::system_error, so catch that and log
the same message.

Tested by cross-compiling with Boost 1.90 and GCC 15 (Yocto wrynose).

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/autowarefoundation/autoware_universe/pull/13591]
Signed-off-by: Ahmed Adel Wafdy <fandes99@gmail.com>
